WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.300
You can create timed promotional offers with Amazon deals, an invite-only program that helps you

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:11.118
offer discounts to customers on eligible ASINs.

00:00:11.118 --> 00:00:14.740
There are two types of deals available in the

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:17.622
Amazon store, Lightning Deals and Best deals.

00:00:17.622 --> 00:00:21.740
Lightning deals run for 4 to 12 hours and are

00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:26.173
ideal when you want to create urgency and drive quick sales with a deep discount.

00:00:26.173 --> 00:00:27.060
They work best

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:31.220
for clearing excess inventory and selling seasonal products.

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:34.340
Best deals run for a limited

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:37.500
number of days or throughout an entire high-velocity event.

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:39.080
These are best suited for

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:43.880
products where you have enough inventory to run a longer promotion and for seasonal items

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:46.213
that benefit from more visibility.

00:00:46.213 --> 00:00:49.480
Access the deals dashboard to get started.

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:50.880
If this is

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:54.056
your first deal, you'll see the deals benefits page.

00:00:54.056 --> 00:00:56.880
Select Create a New Deal to access the

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:57.259
dashboard.

00:00:57.259 --> 00:01:02.940
Use the search and filtering options and select View on current or past deals to

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:05.580
review performance metrics and deal details.

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:09.980
To create a new deal, select Create a New Deal.

00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:13.008
Here, eligible ASINs are displayed automatically.

00:01:13.008 --> 00:01:16.540
ASIN recommendations are generated on a weekly

00:01:16.540 --> 00:01:16.966
basis.

00:01:16.966 --> 00:01:22.500
If you don't have active ASIN recommendations for deals, consider other promotion types,

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:24.652
such as price discounts or coupons.

00:01:24.652 --> 00:01:28.240
Review the Amazon deals help page to see deal eligibility

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:28.655
requirements.

00:01:28.655 --> 00:01:35.300
You can choose whether you would like to create deals one by one or in bulk.

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:42.820
To create deals in bulk, select Download All Recommendations for up to 1,500 ASIN recommendations

00:01:42.820 --> 00:01:47.323
or use filters to select specific ASINs.

00:01:47.323 --> 00:01:49.897
Then select Download Recommendations.

00:01:49.897 --> 00:01:50.540
You'll

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:56.280
be redirected to the Manage in Bulk page where you can track the status of bulk recommendations.

00:01:56.280 --> 00:02:00.108
Note, template processing may take up to 30 minutes.

00:02:00.108 --> 00:02:02.660
Select Download File from the Downloads

00:02:02.660 --> 00:02:04.609
tab under Recent Activities.

00:02:04.609 --> 00:02:08.020
Complete the spreadsheet template, reviewing the instructions

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:09.727
on the Instructions tab.

00:02:09.727 --> 00:02:14.420
In the Deal Recommendation Template tab, input the deal schedule, review

00:02:14.420 --> 00:02:18.663
offer price, and additional required fields for each Amazon store.

00:02:18.663 --> 00:02:20.360
Once your template is

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:25.908
complete, save the file, then select Upload File from the Manage in Bulk tool.

00:02:25.908 --> 00:02:26.700
If any

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:31.780
issues are detected while uploading, re-download the Recommendation file and go to the Error

00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:32.500
Sheet tab.

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:37.900
Here, you can find a list of the errors made in the previously uploaded file.

00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:41.868
The errors can also be spotted in the Deal Recommendation Template tab.

00:02:41.868 --> 00:02:42.860
Once the errors

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:48.940
are fixed, re-upload the file to continue your deal creation.

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:54.980
To create deals one by one, use the search or filtering options to locate eligible ASINs

00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:55.962
and choose Select.

00:02:55.962 --> 00:03:00.220
Select the Amazon stores and audience you want your deal to be eligible

00:03:00.220 --> 00:03:00.535
for.

00:03:00.535 --> 00:03:02.742
Next, select a schedule for your deal.

00:03:02.742 --> 00:03:05.580
You will see a list of available weeks that

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:06.888
your deal can run.

00:03:06.888 --> 00:03:08.851
Review the fee for your deal.

00:03:08.851 --> 00:03:11.140
Fees may change based on several factors,

00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:12.470
such as timing.

00:03:12.470 --> 00:03:16.460
Finally, configure your deal, selecting any eligible product variations

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:19.720
of this ASIN that you want to include.

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:22.980
We recommend including as many variations as possible.

00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:27.317
Set offer prices and discounts and adjust committed units if required.

00:03:27.317 --> 00:03:28.500
Select a featured

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:30.004
ASIN for your deal.

00:03:30.004 --> 00:03:34.140
Review each section for accuracy, then click Submit Deal to submit

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:35.458
the deal for review.

00:03:35.458 --> 00:03:39.081
Go to the deals dashboard in Seller Central to get started.

00:03:39.081 --> 00:03:39.740
For additional

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:42.400
guidance, visit the Create a Deal Help page.
